  "blocked_reason": "Missing numeric ex vivo scores for T3 (Paclitaxel/Carboplatin) and T9 (Somatostatin) in the provided supplementary tables; no binary classification threshold or AUC value reported in the text. Additionally, T5 has no post-dissection treatment listed in Table 1 (R6C8 is '–'), making clinical truth assignment ambiguous for the ex vivo test."
 },
 "notes": [
  "The article reports 'compelling correlations' but does not provide a specific statistical metric (e.g., AUC, Accuracy) for the clinical prediction performance in the main text or tables.",
  "Supplementary Figure 5 provides viability reduction data for specific drugs, but not all clinical regimens are represented by a single matching ex vivo test. For example, T3 received Paclitaxel+Carboplatin clinically, but Fig 5 does not list this combination for T3. T9 received Somatostatin, which is not listed in Fig 5 rows.",
  "Truth values were derived from Table 1: 'Remission', 'Partial remission', 'Stable disease' mapped to 1 (Response); 'Deterioration', 'No response', 'Deceased' mapped to 0 (Non-response). T5 has '–' for post-dissection treatment, so truth is undefined/missing for a clinical comparison.",
  "Ex vivo scores are 'Viability reduction'. Higher reduction (higher score) indicates sensitivity. T1 Oxaliplatin value is 0.87. Text says '~90% reduction'. This confirms higher score = higher sensitivity.",
  "T2 had stable disease with Etoposide-containing regimen. Ex vivo Etoposide score is -0.47 (negative reduction, i.e., growth). This is a discordance noted in the records."
 ]
